  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\n   - Employ a genetic algorithm to explore the solution space more thoroughly and avoid local optima. This is suitable for the non-convex problem and leverages populations to find better optima.\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n   - Represent h as a discretized vector over [0, 2] with n_points samples.\n   - Objective: Minimize max_correlation(h, 1 - h) * dx.\n   - Constraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 and sum(h) = n_points / 2.\n   - Use FFT for efficient correlation computation.\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n   a. Initialize population with 50 individuals including initial_h_values and structured templates.\n   b. Evaluate each individual using FFT-based overlap integral calculation.\n   c. Select top 50% based on lowest C5.\n   d. Perform crossover and mutation to generate new individuals.\n   e. Enforce constraints post-mutation via clipping and rescaling.\n   f. Repeat until budget exhausted, then select best candidate.\n\n4. Search choices and variations:\n   -\u4eba\u53e3\u5927\u5c0f\uff1a\u4ece50\u5f00\u59cb\uff0c\u6839\u636e\u6027\u80fd\u8c03\u6574\u3002\n   -\u53d8\u5f02\u7387\uff1a\u521d\u59cb\u8bbe\u7f6e\u4e3a5%\uff0c\u5982\u679c\u51fa\u73b0\u505c\u6ede\u5219\u589e\u52a0\u3002\n   -\u57fa\u56e0\u91cd\u7ec4\u7b56\u7565\uff1a\u4f7f\u7528\u5355\u70b9\u4ea4\u53c9\uff0c\u5e76\u5c1d\u8bd5\u5747\u5300\u4ea4\u53c9\u3002\n   -\u521d\u59cb\u5316\u6a21\u677f\uff1a\u5305\u62ec\u5747\u5300\u3001\u4e09\u89d2\u5f62\u548c\u6b63\u5f26\u6ce2\u521d\u59cb\u5316\u3002\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness:\n   - Budget allocation: 1100s, with most time spent on correlation evaluations.\n   - Use FFT optimizations and dynamic adaptation of population size and mutation rates.\n\n6. Validation and return contract:\n   - Ensure sum(h) = n_points / 2 and all h[i] \u2208 [0,1].\n   - Recompute max overlap for final candidate.\n   - Return best feasible solution found within the budget.",
